BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Polytope Memory: Jie Ma-traditional Chinese flute\, Brian Foreman-
 percussion and Prof. Brian Saia-sound design
DTSTART:20260910T233000
DTEND:20260911T003000
DTSTAMP:20260903T152848Z
UID:cc48f37113852174efb5dadfaee5e3@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Memory is a concert curated for Polytope Music's 2026 residenc
 y program at Holy Cross. An immersive\, interactive work featuring Jie Ma
 \, pipa player (traditional Chinese lute)\, Brian Foreman\, percussionist 
 and electronic musician\, and Professor Brian Saia\, sound designer. Where
  thousands of years of eastern tradition meet music technology\, it's an e
 vening that asks the question: what does it mean to remember through sound
 ? The performance is the culmination of a residency that brings Polytope M
 usic into the classroom\, where students work alongside the artists to exp
 lore how tradition and technology can be woven into living sound. As the p
 ast speaks to the present\, Memory does what music has always done best 
 — it draws us toward connection across generations and cultures\, time a
 nd space. Funded by The Patrick E. Moriarty\, M.D. '57 Visiting Scholars P
 rogram Dress Code: Casual (jeans ok) --- Event Details: https://myhc.holyc
 ross.edu/rsvp?id=2152224\n\nSource: College of the Holy Cross\nEvent page:
  https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152224
LOCATION:Boroughs Theatre\, Prior\, 1 College Street\, Worcester\, MA 0161
 0\, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152224
END:VEVENT
