BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Constitution Day Lecture
DTSTART:20260923T170000
DTEND:20260923T183000
DTSTAMP:20260903T152849Z
UID:55fd59ea5c1c36438b0a4a2054ab4d@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:The United States Constitution was signed on September 17\, 17
 87\, and in honor of that day in American history\, the Political Science 
 department hosts an annual Constitution Day lecture on or near the anniver
 sary. This year\, we will welcome Dr. Matthew Spalding\, dean of the Van A
 ndel Graduate School of Government at Hillsdale College\, to speak about h
 is new book\, The Making of the American Mind: The Story of Our Declaratio
 n of Independence. The official response will be from Noah Laren ’24. Th
 is event will be held on Wednesday\, September 23\, at 5:00 p.m. in the Cu
 rtis Performance Hall. This event is part of Assumption’s year-long seri
 es celebrating the 250th anniversary of the Declaration of Independence\, 
 Striving for Life\, Liberty\, and the Pursuit of Happiness.\n\nSource: Ass
 umption University\nEvent page: https://www.assumption.edu/news-and-events
 /events/constitution-day-lecture
LOCATION:Curtis Performance Hall\, Tsotsis Family Academic Center\, 500 Sa
 lisbury Street\, Worcester\, MA\, 01609
URL:https://www.assumption.edu/news-and-events/events/constitution-day-lec
 ture
END:VEVENT
