DTEND:20261006T220000
DTSTAMP:20260903T152849Z
UID:69b7560306ac48393cc31c50495fb1@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Be a Squirrel Scout with Holy Cross Libraries! Start in the Di
 nand Library Conference Room (1st floor\, in the Nevins Collection wing) t
 o pick up your instructions and a scavenger hunt. Then\, take your smartph
 one around campus and photograph any squirrels you see! When you're done\,
  come back to the conference room for your Squirrel Scout badge. Photograp
 hs are taken and uploaded in the app iNaturalist to contribute to the Squi
 rrel Mapper project (https://www.squirrelmapper.org/)\, a scientific study
  of color evolution in Eastern gray squirrels that is powered by volunteer
  citizen scientist contributions. You may want to download the app iNatura
 list (https://www.inaturalist.org/projects/squirrelmapper) and make an acc
 ount before the event. This event is part of the Seeds of Knowledge series
 . For more events and information\, visit https://libguides.holycross.edu/
 seedsofknowledge. --- Event Details: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=21
 53032\n\nSource: College of the Holy Cross\nEvent page: https://myhc.holyc
 ross.edu/rsvp?id=2153032
LOCATION:Dinand Library Conference Room\, 1st Floor Nevins Wing\, One Coll
 ege Street\, Worcester\, Mass 01610\, United States
