BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BUDGETING: UNDERSTANDING YOUR INFLOWS AND OUTFLOWS
DTSTART:20261007T220000
DTEND:20261007T231500
DTSTAMP:20260903T152849Z
UID:7ca38031728dcaff818ee9b3caaabc@worcester-colleges
DESCRIPTION:Where does your money go—and how can you make it work harder
  for you? Whether you’re living on financial aid\, a paycheck\, an assis
 tantship\, family support\, or a combination of income sources\, knowing w
 hat comes in and what goes out is an essential part of financial independe
 nce. This workshop will help you build a realistic budget that works with 
 your actual student life—not an imaginary one. We’ll cover: ● Unders
 tanding your income and expenses ● Separating needs\, wants\, and financ
 ial goals ● Managing irregular income and expenses ● Creating a spendi
 ng plan you can actually follow ● Preparing for unexpected expenses ● 
 Finding room to save while still enjoying life Meeting Link: TBD --- Event
  Details: https://mywpi.wpi.edu/rsvp?id=403496\n\nSource: Worcester Polyte
 chnic Institute\nEvent page: https://mywpi.wpi.edu/rsvp?id=403496
LOCATION:Online Event
URL:https://mywpi.wpi.edu/rsvp?id=403496
END:VEVENT
